<title>INDIA: India's Reserve Bank says buys $40 mln on Friday.</title>
<headline>India's Reserve Bank says buys $40 mln on Friday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) bought $40  million from the inter-bank foreign exchange market on Friday, a central  bank spokeswoman told Reuters.  </p>
<p>&quot;We bought $40 million today,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Bankers had earlier said the RBI intervened in the forward dollar  market, helping raise the forward premium levels.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
